{title: To God Be the Glory}
{artist: Fanny Crosby / William Doane}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 104}
{time: 4/4}
{score: to-god-be-the-glory.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]To God be the glory, great [C]things He hath [G]done
So [G]loved He the world that He [D]gave us His [G]Son
Who [G]yielded His life an a[C]tonement for [G]sin
And [G]opened the Life-gate that [D]all may go [G]in
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [D]earth hear His voice
[D]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [G]people re[D]joice
O [G]come to the Father, through [C]Jesus the [G]Son
And [G]give Him the glory, great [D]things He hath [G]done
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]O perfect redemption, the [C]purchase of [G]blood
To [G]every believer the [D]promise of [G]God
The [G]vilest offender who [C]truly be[G]lieves
That [G]moment from Jesus a [D]pardon re[G]ceives
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Great things He hath taught us, great [C]things He hath [G]done
And [G]great our rejoicing through [D]Jesus the [G]Son
But [G]purer, and higher, and [C]greater will [G]be
Our [G]wonder, our transport, when [D]Jesus we [G]see
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
